From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:21:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ag71xx: fix the 10 Mbit/s RGMII/MII clock

The phase counters of ETH_XMII_CONTROL hold the number of CLK100 cycles
in each half of the interface clock, minus one (QCA9558 datasheet,
10.6.18, describes them as "CLK100/CLK125 + 1" cycles). At 100 Mbit/s,
0x01 gives 2 cycles, 20 ns, and the 25 MHz clock. At 10 Mbit/s, the
2.5 MHz clock needs 20 cycles, 0x13, but 0x16 gives 23 cycles and
2.17 MHz.

Use 0x13, which the OpenWrt device trees of the AeroHive HiveAP-121
and Meraki MR18 and Z1 already set, as does the 8devices Rambutan for
the same clock of its SGMII MAC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx.c
@@ -1044,8 +1044,8 @@ static void ag71xx_xmii_set_speed(struct
 		       FIELD_PREP(ETH_XMII_PHASE0_CNT, 0x01);
 		break;
 	case SPEED_10:
-		val |= FIELD_PREP(ETH_XMII_PHASE1_CNT, 0x16) |
-		       FIELD_PREP(ETH_XMII_PHASE0_CNT, 0x16);
+		val |= FIELD_PREP(ETH_XMII_PHASE1_CNT, 0x13) |
+		       FIELD_PREP(ETH_XMII_PHASE0_CNT, 0x13);
 		break;
 	}
 
